{"data": [{"author_id": "1887151146", "created_at": "2026-11-06T04:10:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118555936147345630", "2118556111385280814", "2118556606489374783"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "1891523745929732096", "start": 16, "username": "thinkymachines"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "arxiv.org/pdf/2610.24206", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.24206", "start": 243, "status": 200, "unwound_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.24206", "url": "https://t.co/wJbsizsuOs"}, {"display_url": "x.com/thinkymachines…", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thinkymachines/status/2118489527362912566", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we"}]}, "id": "2118556606489374783", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 802, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118489527362912566", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Congrats to the @thinkymachines team on the release of Inkling 2 Small! Strong results for a smaller model, and another example of SWE-bench Pro V2 helping benchmark the next generation of smaller, more capable models.\n\n- SWE-Bench Pro Paper: https://t.co/wJbsizsuOs\n- https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we", "url": "https://x.com/liuying04/status/2118556606489374783"}, {"author_id": "1887151146", "created_at": "2026-11-06T04:07:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118555936147345630", "2118556111385280814", "2118556606489374783"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "1891523745929732096", "start": 16, "username": "thinkymachines"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/thinkymachines…", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thinkymachines/status/2118489527362912566", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we"}]}, "id": "2118555936147345630", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118489527362912566", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Congrats to the @thinkymachines team on the release of Inkling 2 Small! Strong results for a smaller model, and another example of SWE-bench Pro V2 helping benchmark the next generation of smaller, more capable models.\n\nSWE-Bench Pro Paper: https:/arxiv.org/pdf/2610.24206 https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we", "url": "https://x.com/liuying04/status/2118555936147345630"}, {"author_id": "1887151146", "created_at": "2026-11-06T04:08:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118555936147345630", "2118556111385280814", "2118556606489374783"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "1891523745929732096", "start": 16, "username": "thinkymachines"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/thinkymachines…", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thinkymachines/status/2118489527362912566", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we"}]}, "id": "2118556111385280814", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118489527362912566", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Congrats to the @thinkymachines team on the release of Inkling 2 Small! Strong results for a smaller model, and another example of SWE-bench Pro V2 helping benchmark the next generation of smaller, more capable models.\n\n- SWE-Bench Pro Paper: https:/arxiv.org/pdf/2610.24206\n- https://t.co/aLNX6fu1we", "url": "https://x.com/liuying04/status/2118556111385280814"}, {"author_id": "138143310", "created_at": "2026-11-06T02:47:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118535757761831077"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Karpathy’s 2017 joke became a benchmark result. On test-verifiable coding tasks, models now solve what looked impossible; the bottleneck moved to verification.", "display_url": "sesamedisk.com/gradient-desce…", "end": 243, "expanded_url": "https://sesamedisk.com/gradient-descent-learned-to-code/", "images": [{"height": 709, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118535765386985472/0pVKhbfw?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1260}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118535765386985472/0pVKhbfw?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 220, "status": 200, "title": "Gradient Descent Learned to Code", "unwound_url": "https://sesamedisk.com/gradient-descent-learned-to-code/", "url": "https://t.co/f9khcNw0GR"}]}, "id": "2118535757761831077", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Karpathy's 2017 joke that gradient descent can write code now has a benchmark: SWE-bench Verified systems reached about 80% by late 2025, up from SWE-agent's 12.47% in March 2024. Tests only measure what they can check. https://t.co/f9khcNw0GR", "url": "https://x.com/abel_aguzmans/status/2118535757761831077"}, {"author_id": "1443195228165447680", "created_at": "2026-11-07T10:31:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119014782133055519"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Ricursive Intelligence is releasing Ripple-65B Preview, a 65-billion-parameter open-weight language model that the company says achieves the top score among open-source U.S. models on the TerminalBench 2.1 coding benchmark at a total R&D cost of $32 million. On other benchmarks, however, Ripple falls behind the likewise newly released western open model Inkling 2 Small.", "display_url": "shorturl.at/yq3Kc", "end": 57, "expanded_url": "https://shorturl.at/yq3Kc", "start": 34, "status": 200, "title": "Ripple-65B Preview delivers strong agentic coding results as a fully Apache 2.0 open US model", "unwound_url": "https://the-decoder.com/ripple-65b-preview-delivers-strong-agentic-coding-results-as-a-fully-apache-2-0-open-us-model/", "url": "https://t.co/xPNbuuB5JK"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/M1dNiOgtRU", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ApollonVisual/status/2119014782133055519/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119014723312132096", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/M1dNiOgtRU"}]}, "id": "2119014782133055519", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Ripple-65B Preview Open US Model\n\nhttps://t.co/xPNbuuB5JK\n\nRicursive Intelligence released Ripple-65B Preview a 65 billion parameter open weight language model. \n\nThe model was pretrained on 12 trillion tokens. \n\nRicursive reports a score of 80.52 on the TerminalBench 2.1 coding https://t.co/M1dNiOgtRU", "url": "https://x.com/ApollonVisual/status/2119014782133055519"}, {"author_id": "3023793775", "created_at": "2026-11-07T00:35:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118864970385424763"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/CRjyedqsZU", "end": 228, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/pdurdenj/status/2118864970385424763/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118864967872970752", "start": 205, "url": "https://t.co/CRjyedqsZU"}]}, "id": "2118864970385424763", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "&gt;be me\n&gt;new model tops every benchmark\n&gt;23 tweet thread, \"this changes everything\"\n&gt;move whole company over\n&gt;ask it to fix a typo\n&gt;it rewrites the repo in rust\n&gt;mfw 94.2% on SWE-bench https://t.co/CRjyedqsZU", "url": "https://x.com/pdurdenj/status/2118864970385424763"}, {"author_id": "2059899645854375936", "created_at": "2026-11-06T15:34:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118728762263273941"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/EinsiaAI/statu…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/EinsiaAI/status/2118716282971599349", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/BLhrAv2sr1"}]}, "id": "2118728762263273941", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 74, "impression_count": 8323, "like_count": 109, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 78, "retweet_count": 81}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118716282971599349", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Frontier3DBench could become a major benchmark for 3D coding agents, much like SWE-bench did for software.\nIt covers 145 tasks across Blender and UE5, testing 11 model setups on appearance, structure, and behavior.\nNo model has mastered every category yet, especially when it https://t.co/BLhrAv2sr1", "url": "https://x.com/Emma_Sterling12/status/2118728762263273941"}, {"author_id": "1639838142", "created_at": "2026-11-07T17:15:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119116457544221112"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/loresjpg/statu…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/loresjpg/status/2118880329490637049", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/Cf7vQMdH6Z"}]}, "id": "2119116457544221112", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 215, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118880329490637049", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "models that tie on a benchmark stop tying when you nudge the task.\n\njustin lo built maxxbench, 89 deepswe tasks with small changes to the instructions or starting code. by his numbers, models clustered around 74% on deepswe end up 23 points apart.\n\ndeedy says only opus 5.5 scored https://t.co/Cf7vQMdH6Z", "url": "https://x.com/perperp_er/status/2119116457544221112"}, {"author_id": "112778517", "created_at": "2026-11-07T09:12:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118994956761108673"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 9, "start": 0, "tag": "ARCPrize"}, {"end": 212, "start": 195, "tag": "ThinkingMachines"}, {"end": 217, "start": 213, "tag": "LLM"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/arcprize/statu…", "end": 241, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arcprize/status/2118788850742911073", "start": 218, "url": "https://t.co/HkO1KxKHjZ"}]}, "id": "2118994956761108673", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118788850742911073", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "#ARCPrize reports 81.7% on ARC-AGI-2 at $0.27 per task for Inkling 2 Small. Useful evidence—but benchmark cost is only one part of deployment cost. Watch reproducibility when the weights arrive. #ThinkingMachines #LLM https://t.co/HkO1KxKHjZ", "url": "https://x.com/Cult_Of_Token/status/2118994956761108673"}, {"author_id": "1773935160192647168", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:33:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118758583836049421"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 44, "id": "711048242147041280", "start": 28, "username": "kenneth0stanley"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/nJapJO3vRO", "end": 198, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/arcprize/status/2118758583836049421/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118484345459810304", "start": 175, "url": "https://t.co/nJapJO3vRO"}]}, "id": "2118758583836049421", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 9368, "like_count": 67, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "ARC Prize Research Summit - @kenneth0stanley\n\nOn why open-endedness, invention, discovery are essential to AGI, but designing a benchmark for them creates difficult problems. https://t.co/nJapJO3vRO", "url": "https://x.com/arcprize/status/2118758583836049421"}, {"author_id": "2083951544618352640", "created_at": "2026-11-06T08:45:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118625716992414001"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/X7c96NrZCr", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/hfcxgexf/status/2118625716992414001/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118625714098376704", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/X7c96NrZCr"}]}, "id": "2118625716992414001", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "New ARC-AGI-3 leaderboard: GPT-6 Astra tops at 99.9%, Gemini 4 Argon right behind at 97.5%. These are interactive games where the agent learns the rules from scratch — no instructions. The gap at the top is now razor thin. Benchmark season never ends. NFA/DYOR https://t.co/X7c96NrZCr", "url": "https://x.com/hfcxgexf/status/2118625716992414001"}, {"author_id": "1963124452390297600", "created_at": "2026-11-06T10:27:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118651498532049230"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/zJtuZmxBwG", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/bebuu_ai/status/2118651498532049230/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118651478936367104", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/zJtuZmxBwG"}]}, "id": "2118651498532049230", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 547, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Two new benchmark breakdowns for Gemini 4 Argon dropped today:\n\n- On ARC-AGI-3 (interactive games where agents learn the rules from scratch with zero instructions), Gemini 4 Argon scored 97.5%, second only to GPT-6 Astra at 99.9%\n- On the 19-model SuperCLUE Nov 2026 benchmark, https://t.co/zJtuZmxBwG", "url": "https://x.com/bebuu_ai/status/2118651498532049230"}, {"author_id": "1265140425406414853", "created_at": "2026-11-07T11:15:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119025836913311935"], "id": "2119025836913311935", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 143, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "# 65B That Outperformed 501B: Inside Ripple-65B's $32 Million Bet Against Scale\n\nThe large language model industry has spent the last two years moving in one direction: more parameters, more experts, more money. Ricursive Intelligence went the other way. Their Ripple-65B", "url": "https://x.com/VitaliiKhomenk1/status/2119025836913311935"}, {"author_id": "2052153860299624448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T14:50:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118717789422911567"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "AI agents may consume massive tokens across a wide range of tasks, but how many of those tokens are really necessary? Although prior work has shown that agents can incur unexpectedly high token...", "display_url": "arxiv.org/abs/2611.07238", "end": 103, "expanded_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.07238", "images": [{"height": 1000, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118717790815473664/8q3HHmDT?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118717790815473664/8q3HHmDT?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 80, "status": 200, "title": "How Do AI Agents Waste Your Money?", "unwound_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.07238", "url": "https://t.co/Q4NAm0pIbl"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/LbHcgTPupc", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/arkyyang/status/2118717789422911567/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118717740852899841", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/LbHcgTPupc"}]}, "id": "2118717789422911567", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 425, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"How Do AI Agents Waste Your Money?\" — new paper (arXiv preprint, Nov 4, 2026). https://t.co/Q4NAm0pIbl\n\nIn plain terms: AI providers bill by the token (a small chunk of text, roughly three-quarters of a word), and an agent run can burn millions of them. This paper measures how https://t.co/LbHcgTPupc", "url": "https://x.com/arkyyang/status/2118717789422911567"}, {"author_id": "2110645372347371520", "created_at": "2026-11-06T20:36:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118804818399793541"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/s3MRnZYrMH", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BercusNA/status/2118804818399793541/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118799318123499520", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/s3MRnZYrMH"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Davidstout/sta…", "end": 327, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Davidstout/status/2118035011236397350", "start": 304, "url": "https://t.co/gdLOTaT6cU"}]}, "id": "2118804818399793541", "public_metrics":